\fs21 \cf8 \cb3 \strokec8 The wings scorched by the blazing sun once fell to the pale earth, into a lightless chasm.\cb1 \
\cb3 Then fall... She will bear it all. The weight, the darkness, those defiant follies, those lives that slipped away...\cb1 \
\cb3 In that long slumber forgotten by time, even sorrow faded away. Pain and despair faded too... As did joy. As did memory. All withered away, for all is vanity.\cb1 \
\cb3 A hundred years passed in the blink of an eye. Kingdoms upon the earth fell and rose anew, yet she never awoke.\cb1 \
\cb3 But no matter how much unspeakable darkness lay buried within her heart, a bird cannot pretend not to see the coming of spring.\cb1 \
\
\cb3 "Spring flowers are winter's dream, and autumn clouds remember the summer breeze~"\cb1 \
\cb3 \'97Beneath the quiet moonlit sky, a pink-haired girl softly hums an ancient nursery rhyme.\cb1 \
